Done. #1117 is fixed and committed as d8988d05, and build, clippy, fmt and the full cargo test all pass.

The cause wasn't where the plan said. openrouter_anthropic_preset_id already turned the dashed anthropic/claude-opus-4-6 into claude-opus-4-6. The miss came after that. yoyo's anthropic_preset has no entry for opus 4-6, and shouldn't get one, since yoagent's price table now holds those limits. The fallback, ModelConfig::preset("openrouter", ..), only accepts OpenRouter's dotted spelling.

The fix: a new providers::openrouter_routed_preset. When yoagent turns down the dashed form, it retries with the dotted form, using yoagent's own spelling rule (a trailing -4-6 becomes -4.6). So a dashed id works exactly when its dotted twin does, and there's no list of opus versions to maintain. :batch-style variants are never respelled, and other vendors' ids are left to yoagent. The openrouter branch in agent_builder.rs calls it. That's a one-line change in a file the plan's Files: line didn't list, but that's where the lookup runs.

Before/after, measured with the built binary (1 = warns that yoyo is guessing the model's limits):

| id | before | after |
|---|---|---|
| opus-4-7 / 4-6 / 4-5 (dashed) | 1 | 0 |
| opus 4.7 / 4.6 / 4.5 (dotted) | 0 | 0 |
| sonnet 4.5, opus 4.1 (both spellings) | 1 | 1 |
| sonnet-4.6:batch | 1 | 1 |

The probe has to run from an empty directory. This repo's .yoyo.toml sets max_tokens, which silences the warning, so my first run from inside the repo showed 0 for every id.

The ids that still warn do so on purpose:
• Sonnet 4.5 and Opus 4.1: Anthropic retired Opus 4.1 and is retiring Sonnet 4.5, and yoagent deliberately has no entry for them. yoyo really is guessing, so the warning is true.
• `:batch`: this is OpenRouter's half-price variant. Giving it the full-price entry would make /cost show double. I added it to #1012, the pricing ticket.

Pricing: /cost already priced both spellings the same, using yoagent's price table, so format/cost.rs is unchanged. A new test checks that they stay the same.

Tests: I added four tests in src/openrouter_preset_tests.rs. The expected limits are read from yoagent, not typed in, and there are near-miss cases for the ids that must keep warning. As a check, I pointed the fallback back at the user's own dashed id: the two dashed-id tests failed by name. I restored it in the same command and they pass again.

Docs and tickets: I updated docs/src/configuration/models.md to say which Claude ids still warn and why. I commented on #1012 (the :batch scope) and #1117 (the closing reasons). git grep '#1117' finds only comments recording where the code came from, with no user-facing "tracked in" pointers to rewrite.

